20261002/P00/accounting-dossier-checks.json\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/preflight-20261002/P00/check_accounting_dossiers.py.log\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T154913-29ec15cd/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T153509-a6196216/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T161508-4840af1a/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T162132-34d40f0a/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T172827-eae82272/manifest.json\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,240p' scripts/build_real_case.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# AccDSL project instructions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Mission entry point\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\\\\\\\\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\\\\\\\\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\\\\\\\\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\\\\\\\\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\\\\\\\\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\\\\\\\\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\\\\\\\\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\\\\\\\\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\\\\\\\\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\\\\\\\\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\\\\\\\\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\\\\\\\\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Working rules\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\\\\\\\\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\\\\\\\\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\\\\\\\\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\\\\\\\\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\\\\\\\\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\\\\\\\\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\\\\\\\\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\\\\\\\\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\\\\\\\\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\\\\\\\\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\\\\\\\\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\\\\\\\\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\\\\\\\\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\\\\\\\\n- Follow the applicable policies under\\\\\\\\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\\\\\\\\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\\\\\\\\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\\\\\\\\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\\\\\\\\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\\\\\\\\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\\\\\\\\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\\\\\\\\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\\\\\\\\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\\\\\\\\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\\\\\\\\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\\\\\\\\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\\\\\\\\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\\\\\\\\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\\\\\\\\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\\\\\\\\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\\\\\\\\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,240p' scripts/build_real_case.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Inventory the acquired Apple package; retain unresolved semantic obligations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\\\\\nimport json\\\\\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\\\\\nimport re\\\\\\\\nimport shutil\\\\\\\\nimport subprocess\\\\\\\\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup, NavigableString\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\\\\\\\nOUT=ROOT/'docs/design/cases/apple'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef digest(p):return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef main():\\\\\\\\n    OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\\\\\\\\n    sources=[('annual-2024.pdf','/tmp/accdsl-apple-2024.pdf','https://www.annualreports.com/HostedData/AnnualReportArchive/a/NASDAQ_AAPL_2024.pdf'),\\\\\\\\n             ('interim-2025q1.html','/tmp/accdsl-apple-q1.html','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000008/aapl-20241228.htm')]\\\\\\\\n    documents=[]\\\\\\\\n    for name,temp,url in sources:\\\\\\\\n        target=OUT/name\\\\\\\\n        if not target.exists():shutil.copyfile(temp,target)\\\\\\\\n        documents.append(dict(id=name,url=url,local_path=str(target.relative_to(ROOT)),sha256=digest(target),access_date='2026-10-02',availability_precision='filing day; exact EDGAR acceptance time not established here'))\\\\\\\\n    subprocess.run(['pdftotext','-layout',str(OUT/'annual-2024.pdf'),str(OUT/'annual-2024.txt')],check=True)\\\\\\\\n    annual=(OUT/'annual-2024.txt').read_text();pages=annual.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f');pages=pages[:-1] if not pages[-1].strip() else pages\\\\\\\\n    soup=BeautifulSoup((OUT/'interim-2025q1.html').read_text(),'html.parser')\\\\\\\\n    for el in soup(['script','style']):el.decompose()\\\\\\\\n    interim=soup.get_text('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n',strip=True);(OUT/'interim-2025q1.txt').write_text(interim)\\\\\\\\n    # Page accounting is distinct from note inventory and structured observations.\\\\\\\\n    page_units=[]\\\\\\\\n    for i,p in enumerate(pages,1):\\\\\\\\n        footer=re.search(r'Apple Inc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\. \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\| 2024 Form 10-K \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\| (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)',p)\\\\\\\\n        printed=int(footer.group(1)) if footer else None\\\\\\\\n        disposition='financial_disclosure_retained' if printed and 28<=printed<=50 else 'context_or_exhibit_retained'\\\\\\\\n        page_units.append(dict(id='annual.page.'+str(i),pdf_page=i,printed_page=printed,text_sha256=hashlib.sha256(p.encode()).hexdigest(),disposition=disposition,semantic_status='partially_structured' if printed in [31,38,43,44] else 'not_fully_formalised'))\\\\\\\\n    obligations={\\\\\\\\n        'Summary of Significant Accounting Policies':'Calendar, consolidation and FIFO policy recorded; complete policy-to-rule conversion pending.',\\\\\\\\n        'Basis of Presentation and Preparation':'Interim/annual linkage retained; all preparation qualifications require review before broader simulation.',\\\\\\\\n        'Revenue':'Product/service and segment classifications overlap; performance obligations, deferrals, returns and transaction-price models pending.',\\\\\\\\n        'Earnings Per Share':'Dated basic/diluted share denominators retained; dilution calculation unsupported in this marginal stress.',\\\\\\\\n        'Financial Instruments':'Interest-rate notional and hedge link structured; instrument schedules, valuation and OCI recycling remain unresolved.',\\\\\\\\n        'Property, Plant and Equipment':'Gross/net bridge retained; asset-cohort ages and future depreciation not reconstructed.',\\\\\\\\n        'Consolidated Financial Statement Details':'Detailed balances retained; component movement models and recognition rules pending.',\\\\\\\\n        'Condensed Consolidated Financial Statement Details':'Detailed balances retained; component movement models pending.',\\\\\\\\n        'Income Taxes':'Current/deferred/state-aid effects retained; no tax effect assumed only in the explicitly conditional marginal stress.',\\\\\\\\n        'Leases':'Maturities and policy retained; discounting, modifications and rent forecasts unmodelled.',\\\\\\\\n        'Debt':'Principal/carrying/fair value and dates separated; rate/reset/hedge state incompletely disclosed.',\\\\\\\\n        'Shareholders’ Equity':'Repurchase authorisation is permission, not an obligatory future cash outflow; quantities and reserves retained.',\\\\\\\\n        'Share-Based Compensation':'Vesting/award terms and cash-tax settlements retained; compensation/dilution simulation unmodelled.',\\\\\\\\n        'Commitments, Contingencies and Supply Concentrations':'Qualitative/conditional obligations retained; no unsupported numeric haircut or probability.',\\\\\\\\n        'Segment Information and Geographic Data':'Overlapping product/geography aggregation retained; no cross-axis summation.'}\\\\\\\\n    notes=[]\\\\\\\\n    for doc,text in [('annual',annual),('interim',interim)]:\\\\\\\\n        # Headings at line start distinguish actual notes from in-text references.\\\\\\\\n        pattern=r'(?m)^[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t]*Note (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[–-]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*([^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n]+)'\\\\\\\\n        matches=list(re.finditer(pattern,text))\\\\\\\\n        for j,m in enumerate(matches):\\\\\\\\n            title=m.group(2).strip(); start=m.start();end=matches[j+1].start() if j+1<len(matches) else len(text)\\\\\\\\n            # Last note ends before the auditor/MD&A rather than incorporating the rest of the filing.\\\\\\\\n            tail=text[start:end]\\\\\\\\n            for marker in ['Report of Independent Registered','Item 2.','Item 2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n']:\\\\\\\\n                off=tail.find(marker)\\\\\\\\n                if off>0:end=min(end,start+off)\\\\\\\\n            notes.append(dict(id=doc+'.note.'+m.group(1),number=int(m.group(1)),title=title,\\\\\\\\n                source=doc,start_character=start,end_character=end,\\\\\\\\n                pdf_page=text[:start].count('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\f')+1 if doc=='annual' else None,\\\\\\\\n                disposition='retained_with_specific_obligation',\\\\\\\\n                modelling_obligation=obligations.get(title,'Source text retained; detailed interpretation and operation mapping pending.'),\\\\\\\\n                internal_note_targets=sorted(set(re.findall(r'Note\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)',text[start:end])))))\\\\\\\\n    # Every nonempty text leaf survives. This is segmentation evidence, not visual/OCR accuracy.\\\\\\\\n    leaves=[x for x in soup.descendants if isinstance(x,NavigableString) and x.strip()]\\\\\\\\n    leaf_units=[dict(id='interim.text.'+str(i),text=str(x),parent_tag=x.parent.name,\\\\\\\\n                     html_id=x.parent.get('id'),disposition='structured_fact_candidate' if x.parent.name=='ix:nonfraction' else 'retained_unformalised') for i,x in enumerate(leaves)]\\\\\\\\n    (OUT/'interim-source-units.json').write_text(json.dumps(leaf_units,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n')\\\\\\\\n    tagged=[]\\\\\\\\n    keep={'us-gaap:Assets','us-gaap:Liabilities','us-gaap:StockholdersEquity','us-gaap:CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue','us-gaap:LongTermDebtCurrent','us-gaap:LongTermDebtNoncurrent','us-gaap:CommercialPaper'}\\\\\\\\n    for fact in soup.find_all('ix:nonfraction'):\\\\\\\\n        if fact.get('name') in keep:\\\\\\\\n            cid=fact.get('contextref');ctx=soup.find(id=cid)\\\\\\\\n            tagged.append(dict(id=fact.get('id'),concept=fact.get('name'),literal=fact.get_text(),context_ref=cid,context_xml=str(ctx),unit_ref=fact.get('unitref'),decimals=fact.get('decimals'),scale=fact.get('scale'),sign=fact.get('sign'),format=fact.get('format'),status='tagged_reading_preserved; compared with rendered financial-statement text'))\\\\\\\\n    statements=[\\\\\\\\n        dict(date='2023-09-30',cash='29965',assets='352583',liabilities='290437',equity='62146',term_debt='105103',source='annual printed page 31'),\\\\\\\\n        dict(date='2024-09-28',cash='29943',assets='364980',liabilities='308030',equity='56950',term_debt='96662',source='annual printed page 31; Note 9 printed page 43'),\\\\\\\\n        dict(date='2024-12-28',cash='30299',assets='344085',liabilities='277327',equity='66758',term_debt='94804',source='interim printed page 3; Note 6 printed page 10')]\\\\\\\\n    result=dict(documents=documents,scope='All acquired bytes/pages/text leaves retained; selected numerical semantics only; external incorporation closure incomplete',\\\\\\\\n        page_units=page_units,notes=notes,\\\\\\\\n        interim_text_unit_count=len(leaf_units),interim_source_units='interim-source-units.json',tagged_selected_facts=tagged,\\\\\\\\n        annual_items=[dict(item=i,disposition='retained; see source page and note inventory') for i in ['1','1A','1B','1C','2','3','4','5','6','7','7A','8','9','9A','9B','9C','10','11','12','13','14','15','16']],\\\\\\\\n        interim_items=['I.1 financial statements','I.2 MD&A','I.3 market risk','I.4 controls','II.1 legal','II.1A risks','II.2 equity sales/repurchases','II.3 defaults','II.4 mine safety','II.5 other','II.6 exhibits'],\\\\\\\\n        cross_reference_obligations=[\\\\\\\\n            dict(source='annual Note 9',target='annual Note 4',relation='economic financing/hedge relationship; reviewer-created link supported by both notes',status='resolved_in_package'),\\\\\\\\n            dict(source='annual Note 2',target='annual Note 13',relation='literal disaggregated revenue/segment reference',status='resolved_in_package'),\\\\\\\\n            dict(source='interim Note 1',target='annual Note 1',relation='read interim with annual statements',status='resolved_in_package'),\\\\\\\\n            dict(source='annual Part III',target='2025 proxy statement',relation='incorporated by reference',status='not_acquired; blocks complete external-reference closure'),\\\\\\\\n            dict(source='annual exhibit index',target='incorporated prior-filed agreements/exhibits',relation='incorporated documents',status='retained index; external contracts not all acquired')],\\\\\\\\n        statements=statements,units='USD millions; shares separately typed; rounded presentations retain source precision',\\\\\\\\n        debt_measurements=dict(principal='97341',discount_cost_adjustment='-321',hedge_carrying_adjustment='-358',carrying='96662',fair_value_display_billions='88.4',interest_rate_contract_notional='14575',source='annual Note 9 pages 43–44 and Note 4 page 38'),\\\\\\\\n        marginal_stress=dict(start='2024-12-29',horizon_weeks=13,rate_increment='0.02',exposure_assumption='14575',year_fraction='13/52',tax_effect='0',all_other_movements='frozen conditional baseline; not a whole-company forecast',\\\\\\\\n            expected=dict(interest='72.875',cash='30226.125',assets='344012.125',liabilities='277327',equity='66685.125',profit='-72.875',operating_cash_flow='-72.875')))\\\\\\\\n    (OUT/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n')\\\\\\\\n    assert len([n for n in notes if n['source']=='annual'])==13\\\\\\\\n    assert len([n for n in notes if n['source']=='interim'])==10\\\\\\\\n    print(json.dumps(dict(annual_pages=len(pages),notes=len(notes),interim_text_units=len(leaves),selected_tagged_facts=len(tagged))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nif __name__=='__main__':main()\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg --files docs/design/cases/apple data/accounting-master/deliverables tests src; rg -n 'MC01|MC03|MC05|MC16|MC28|G4|G5|G11|G12|G13' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg --files docs/design/cases/apple data/accounting-master/deliverables tests src; rg -n 'MC01|MC03|MC05|MC16|MC28|G4|G5|G11|G12|G13' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"rg: data/accounting-master/deliverables: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\\\\\nrg: src: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\\\\\ntests/__pycache__/test_accounting_master.cpython-311.pyc\\\\\\\\ntests/test_accounting_master.py\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-source-units.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.pdf\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.html\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-program.md:3:Date: 2 October 2026. User authority: create, review and execute a master program for the consolidated gaps, with actual repair, refreshed plans between phases, and reusable upfront approvals. Scope: MC01–MC35 and G1–G18; the existing mission remains authoritative.\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:36:to the [initial gap audit](../design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md); G11–G18 refer\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:55:| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:61:| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:122:| MC33 | Define meaningful acceptance and separate engineering, accounting and scientific evidence. U3, P, D. | Provide canonical conformance inputs/outputs, corpus/annotation rules, justified release-specific criteria, review status and later forecast baselines/uncertainty protocols. Existing arithmetic/build checks keep their limited meanings. | Specified fixtures, corpus strata, annotation/adjudication/split protocol, hard conformance vetoes and provisional workload limits in Ch. 11/`corpus-protocol.json`. Reference checks, new debt semantic rejection cases, accounting dossiers and author review recorded; the 192-report source panel now passes acquisition acceptance and independent integrity checks. Annotation protocol/schema and provisional family roles exist; adjudication, performance and release validation remain pending. G5, G10. |\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\\\\\\\\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat MISSION_CONTROL.md docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/next-plan.md; sed -n '1,170p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat MISSION_CONTROL.md docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md; cat data/accounting-master/next-plan.md; sed -n '1,170p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# AccDSL mission control\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong) at the user's request.\\\\\\\\nStatus: active mission; Version 1.2 is a repaired design candidate with checked\\\\\\\\nreference cases. Full product, domain and human acceptance remain pending.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Purpose\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDesign a system that represents a company's historical financial disclosures,\\\\\\\\npreserves economically different histories and interpretations compatible with\\\\\\\\nthe evidence, and carries those alternatives into scenario-dependent future\\\\\\\\njournals and financial statements. Preserve their separate conditional outcome\\\\\\\\ndistributions or feasible sets, including uncertainty that cannot be assigned\\\\\\\\ndefensible probabilities.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe immediate deliverable is a detailed, readable LaTeX product and method\\\\\\\\ndesign, with compiled PDF, supporting literature and software investigation,\\\\\\\\nprecise implementation contracts and acceptance examples. The eventual product\\\\\\\\nis the working representation and simulation engine. A document build, a small\\\\\\\\nfinancing example and an implemented prototype are different achievements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Authority and origin\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis mission records the user's existing directions; it does not replace new\\\\\\\\nuser instructions or higher-priority instructions. The three original requests\\\\\\\\nare preserved in saved session `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`, at JSONL\\\\\\\\nrecords 10, 115 and 145. They establish whole-company history, heterogeneous\\\\\\\\naccounting, preservation of alternative journals/outcomes, a broad literature\\\\\\\\nand software survey, and an implementation-governing LaTeX document. The current\\\\\\\\nrequest establishes this durable mission and a requirements-based gap audit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe user's subsequent direction establishes MC35: complete feasible internal\\\\\\\\npreparation before paying for professional review. The user supplied a planning\\\\\\\\nrate of US$500–1,200/hour. This work order is binding; no estimated savings or\\\\\\\\nprofessional engagement is inferred from it.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe [requirements register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\\\\\\\\ndistinguishes direct user requirements from policy obligations and engineering\\\\\\\\nrequirements derived from those goals. Python, storage engines, parser design,\\\\\\\\nsolver libraries and a particular first-company example remain replaceable\\\\\\\\nimplementation proposals. Designing a DSL is part of the work; claiming it is\\\\\\\\nbetter than all alternatives is not a predetermined conclusion.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Main goals\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Goal | Required outcome |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| M1 — Represent the historical record | Preserve annual, quarterly and semi-annual statements, notes, policies and relevant referenced disclosures, with their source, context, temporal meaning and unresolved content. |\\\\\\\\n| M2 — Preserve alternative explanations | Represent joint families of admissible histories, journal movements, contract states and interpretations; distinguish absent facts, accounting choices, estimates and future randomness. |\\\\\\\\n| M3 — Simulate financial evolution | Apply explicit economic scenarios and behaviour to economic state, generate admissible journal entries, and produce coherent future statements and conditional results. |\\\\\\\\n| M4 — Handle accounting and sector diversity | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE, industry and company differences, group boundaries, banks, insurers, liabilities, capital, bonds and equity. |\\\\\\\\n| M5 — Specify implementable methods and language | Define reconstruction, accounting, inference and execution procedures, types, IR, DSL, interfaces, failure behaviour and persistence precisely enough for compatible implementations. |\\\\\\\\n| M6 — Ground choices in research and reusable tools | Inspect primary literature beyond the existing collection and official software, archive relevant sources, compare credible alternatives and document justified inclusion/exclusion and reuse decisions. |\\\\\\\\n| M7 — Deliver the governing design | Produce one rigorous, understandable LaTeX/PDF argument with complete worked cases, explicit scope, source support, method details and an implementation sequence. |\\\\\\\\n| M8 — Establish evidence and maintain direction | Define conformance and release evidence, preserve reproducibility, keep engineering/accounting/scientific conclusions separate, and maintain requirements and open decisions as work proceeds. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Requirements that must survive every implementation choice\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Source preservation is broader than numerical extraction. Account for all\\\\\\\\n   source material within the declared disclosure package, including notes and\\\\\\\\n   cross-references. Content that cannot yet be formalised stays visible with\\\\\\\\n   a reason; it is not silently excluded from a completeness claim.\\\\\\\\n2. Preserve reported assertions, derived consequences and modelling assumptions\\\\\\\\n   separately. A missing value is not zero; a reported number is not automatic\\\\\\\\n   proof of the underlying economic state. Source conflicts remain inspectable.\\\\\\\\n3. Carry entity, group perimeter, concept, dimensions, units, currency, basis,\\\\\\\\n   precision and time through every calculation. Label mapping does not itself\\\\\\\\n   convert between accounting standards. Avoid double counting overlapping\\\\\\\\n   classifications.\\\\\\\\n4. Preserve original and revised information. Economic time, reporting periods,\\\\\\\\n   availability/publication and system ingestion/version time answer different\\\\\\\\n   questions. Historical forecasts cannot use later evidence inadvertently.\\\\\\\\n5. Keep alternatives jointly consistent across statements, notes, dates,\\\\\\\\n   contracts and accounts. Include economic state beyond journals: identical\\\\\\\\n   historical postings can conceal different future exposures.\\\\\\\\n6. Every reconstructed family has an explicit model scope and completeness\\\\\\\\n   status. A selected witness, bounded search or convenient aggregate cannot be\\\\\\\\n   presented as all real histories. Scope exclusions remain mission limitations.\\\\\\\\n7. Preserve conditional results by explanation and scenario. A set or interval\\\\\\\\n   does not become a probability distribution without a declared measure. No\\\\\\\\n   weights from representation counts, arbitrary equality or LLM confidence.\\\\\\\\n   Keep dependence between statement amounts and through time.\\\\\\\\n8. Generate events from explicit contract and behavioural assumptions, then\\\\\\\\n   apply recognition/measurement and posting rules. Balanced journals are\\\\\\\\n   necessary but do not prove accounting treatment or economic correctness.\\\\\\\\n9. Treat unsupported calculations, unresolved branches, numerical failure and\\\\\\\\n   economically meaningful default as distinct outcomes. Do not silently drop\\\\\\\\n   failed branches, manufacture financing or report sampled extrema as exact\\\\\\\\n   bounds.\\\\\\\\n10. Compare a DSL with credible alternatives on the same tasks, especially the\\\\\\\\n    typed-library/shared-IR baseline. Reuse software where its inspected\\\\\\\\n    capabilities fit, with explicit adapter contracts and limits.\\\\\\\\n11. Support imported technical claims with inspected primary sections and local\\\\\\\\n    copies. Preserve relevant papers under `docs/papers` using\\\\\\\\n    `Title First-author-surname (year).pdf`; preserve the original collection.\\\\\\\\n    Technical reading, actual literature screening and source corrections must\\\\\\\\n    be recorded, not inferred from metadata or generated status labels.\\\\\\\\n12. Make assumptions, derivations, scope and limits understandable in the\\\\\\\\n    manuscript itself. Full company cases and precise expected outputs must\\\\\\\\n    connect the concepts to implementation. Page count and polished prose are\\\\\\\\n    not substitutes for these requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## What counts as completion\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe [requirement register](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md)\\\\\\\\ndefines evidence needed for MC01–MC35. Each requirement must have an identified\\\\\\\\ndocument location, stated behaviour/method, a suitable worked case or other\\\\\\\\ncheck, and an honest assessment. A mention is `partial`; promised future work\\\\\\\\nis `open`; a precise design is `specified`; checked evidence can support\\\\\\\\n`checked` within its stated scope. `Not checked` is never silently converted\\\\\\\\nto `passed`. These are design statuses, not implemented-product statuses.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nA proposed implementation-governing design requires:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- complete scope and methods for the declared initial executable profile;\\\\\\\\n- a concrete structural design and method/support obligations for every\\\\\\\\n  explicitly requested domain, including later bank and insurance modules;\\\\\\\\n- source-to-record-to-history-to-journal-to-statement worked cases, with\\\\\\\\n  uncertainty, revisions and failure cases;\\\\\\\\n- exact interfaces and conformance fixtures for the supported language/model;\\\\\\\\n- inspected support for imported claims and explicit disposition of genuine\\\\\\\\n  source gaps;\\\\\\\\n- checked mathematics, references and rendered presentation, with review\\\\\\\\n  records identifying what was and was not checked.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nA source gap blocks its unsupported claim. A missing later engine does not\\\\\\\\nblock the initial core, but a method that is still unspecified remains open\\\\\\\\nin the full design. Do not close the wider mission merely by making a tiny\\\\\\\\nmodel's scope exclude every difficult case. Scope reductions require actual\\\\\\\\nuser direction; routine choices within the scope do not require repeated\\\\\\\\npermission.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nHuman comprehension, independent domain review, executable conformance and\\\\\\\\nscientific forecast validation retain their own pending or completed states.\\\\\\\\nMissing feedback does not block provisional drafting and repair. Do not\\\\\\\\ninvent acceptance or claim a compliant engine from author self-review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Internal preparation before paid review\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFinish feasible internal source retrieval and inspection, fact collection,\\\\\\\\ncalculations, software tests, competing-interpretation analysis and document\\\\\\\\nrepairs before referring a particular question to a professional. “Review\\\\\\\\npending” must not transfer those tasks to an accountant or stop authorised work.\\\\\\\\nSeparate ordinary reader feedback from accounting-firm review. Keep acceptance\\\\\\\\nprovisional where human evidence is still missing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse the [G1–G18 work allocation](docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md)\\\\\\\\nto preserve the internal queue. A possible later question needs a proposed\\\\\\\\nanswer, strongest counterargument, precise authority, complete facts and\\\\\\\\nchecked consequences. The [unsent brief](docs/design/review/future-professional-review-brief.md)\\\\\\\\nprovides question-specific deliverables and a user-chosen fee/time cap for any\\\\\\\\nfuture engagement. No packet is presently declared ready for paid review.\\\\\\\\nMissing current authority, software or actual contract facts are preparation\\\\\\\\ntasks, not generic requests for professional approval.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## How work is controlled\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBefore a nontrivial work unit, identify its MC requirements, current gaps,\\\\\\\\nassumptions and smallest useful validation. Perform the skeptical plan audit\\\\\\\\nrequired by the project policies. Use the existing research-plan/evidence\\\\\\\\nworkflow for actual experiments; document-only edits do not need invented\\\\\\\\nresearch metrics or a performance campaign.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAfter a substantive change, update the affected requirement assessments and\\\\\\\\nthe [checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md). A gap\\\\\\\\ncloses only against its stated evidence. Maintain continuity between the\\\\\\\\noriginal [G1–G10 audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and the\\\\\\\\n[expanded audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md). New findings\\\\\\\\ncan be added; neither list is asserted to be permanently exhaustive. Review\\\\\\\\ninteractions between requirements, not only the rows separately.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUse separate judgements for the document, engineering implementation,\\\\\\\\naccounting validity and scientific interpretation. Follow the applicable\\\\\\\\npolicies in `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`, including scientific\\\\\\\\ncoding, literature audit and natural reader-facing prose. Operational mission\\\\\\\\nrecords belong here, not as repeated administrative scaffolding in the paper.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe user's corpus-first priority has reached source acceptance: panel v2 has\\\\\\\\n192 annual/interim reports across nine issuers, three evidenced accounting\\\\\\\\nfamilies and eight complete years per issuer (2018–2025). Henkel and Munich Re\\\\\\\\nreplace the two inaccessible interim series under the reviewed selection repair;\\\\\\\\nv1 evidence remains preserved. The [corpus result](docs/plans/accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md)\\\\\\\\nand independent integrity manifest record the checks and limitations. Resume\\\\\\\\nfrom that source set, not the former tiny real-company baseline. This closes\\\\\\\\nthe source-collection work unit, not accounting annotations, complete package\\\\\\\\nsemantics, historical availability, implementation or model validation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAfter the source-corpus work, extend the checked authored-debt registry and\\\\\\\\nsemantic validator to the supported Core 0 language and shared-IR compilation,\\\\\\\\nthen the bounded\\\\\\\\nNorthstar reconstruction/execution path. Use the new cases to validate selected\\\\\\\\nadapters. Acquire missing accounting authority and expand the real corpus as\\\\\\\\nbank/insurer and broader standards methods advance. These stages preserve the\\\\\\\\nfull mission; their unimplemented status does not erase the design delivered.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Current assessment and open decisions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe [reviewed repair plan](docs/plans/accounting-gap-repair-2026-10-02.md) has\\\\\\\\nbeen executed as a bounded document/specification campaign. The revised\\\\\\\\n[design](docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf) has 11 chapters and two\\\\\\\\nappendices, a complete synthetic company, a named Apple disclosure case,\\\\\\\\nrounded reconstruction, finite probability examples, corporate/sector cases,\\\\\\\\nCore 0 contracts and acceptance protocols. The [result map](docs/design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md)\\\\\\\\nrecords G1–G18 repairs and remaining obligations. All MC01–MC34 assessments\\\\\\\\nhave been updated without changing their requirement or acceptance wording.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe [internal preparation results](docs/design/review/internal-preparation-results.md)\\\\\\\\nrecord Version 1.2 corrections, a bounded semantic checker, adversarial inputs,\\\\\\\\nthree accounting dossiers, and MC35's standing cost constraint. The original\\\\\\\\n34 technical requirements remain intact; MC35 adds the user's work-order rule.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReference arithmetic, solver, grammar/schema, bounded static and review checks support their\\\\\\\\nstated examples only. The full compiler/runtime and non-Z3 adapters are not\\\\\\\\nimplemented. The real filing has complete acquired-file inventory but partial\\\\\\\\nsemantics and incomplete external incorporation closure. Full ASC authority,\\\\\\\\nofficial-current ASBE verification, richer bank/insurance methods, independent\\\\\\\\naccounting/implementability review and human comprehension remain open.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDecisions now recorded include Northstar/Apple, rational-linear reconstruction,\\\\\\\\nseparate evidence clocks and review actions, deterministic operating assumptions,\\\\\\\\noptional finite weights, schema/identity/storage boundaries, corpus strata and\\\\\\\\nprovisional workload limits. Future measured capacity, production library locks,\\\\\\\\nempirical forecast calibration and corpus adjudication need their own evidence.\\\\\\\\nThe [checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md) preserves\\\\\\\\ncommands, review records and the next justified steps. No scope reduction or\\\\\\\\nwhole-mission completion is implied by this candidate.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNo external deployment, global agent-policy installation, production-security\\\\\\\\nprogramme, full-economy equilibrium model or forecast-superiority claim is\\\\\\\\nimplied by this mission. Such work needs its own substantive justification.\\\\\\\\n# Accounting master checkpoint\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEstablished: 2 October 2026 under the user's create/review/execute instruction.\\\\\\\\nThe executable catalog covers G1–G18 while retaining MC01–MC35 unchanged.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Resume entry point\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRun this exact command, without shell wrappers or environment prefixes:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```text\\\\\\\\npython3 /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/scripts/run_accounting_master.py run\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRead current execution state rather than this installation-time note:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/state.json\\\\\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/next-plan.md\\\\\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/events.jsonl\\\\\\\\n- ../../data/accounting-master/runs/\\\\\\\\n- accounting-master-program.md\\\\\\\\n- ../design/review/accounting-master-review.md\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe status command uses the same prefix and never starts workers. A stop command\\\\\\\\nrequests bounded child termination and preserves partial work. Normal run resumes\\\\\\\\nafter a previous stop. --retry-blocked is reserved for deliberately retrying a\\\\\\\\nknown external block after changed access or environment; ordinary resume does\\\\\\\\nnot repeatedly probe it.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Evidence and scope\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe accepted financial-report corpus remains frozen and source-complete for its\\\\\\\\ndeclared panel. Master outputs go under data/accounting-master; original release\\\\\\\\nhashes are not rewritten to conceal changes. Existing Git remains unusable and\\\\\\\\nhas not been initialised. Prior editable source bytes are retained before phase\\\\\\\\nworkers change them. New source research must preserve provenance and limitations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPlanning, implementation and read-only review run sequentially, with no nested\\\\\\\\nagents. The upfront grant is scoped to this program, its filesystem sandboxes,\\\\\\\\nlegitimate public-source research and project-local work. It does not authorise\\\\\\\\nprofessional fees, paid data/accounts, deployment, outreach or global packages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nA bounded accepted phase does not close its wider accounting/design gap. The\\\\\\\\nrefreshed plan retains residuals and next actions; independent work continues\\\\\\\\nwhile external/human acceptance is pending. P00/P01 preflights passed after a\\\\\\\\nbaseline import-path repair. Full execution and reviewer verdicts are recorded\\\\\\\\nby the runner, not assumed here.\\\\\\\\n# Accounting master — refreshed next plan\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUpdated: 2026-10-02T18:08:00.398719+00:00\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNext eligible phase: P02.\\\\\\\\nMission complete: **no**. Scoped phase acceptance does not close the original gaps.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Phase | State | Residual work |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| P00 — Verify the accepted baseline | accepted_internal | All G1–G18 retain work; bounded reference checks do not establish accounting or forecast validity. |\\\\\\\\n| P01 — Prepare source-context and availability work records | accepted_internal | Publication/version evidence, semantic annotation, incorporated packages and benchmark labels remain open. |\\\\\\\\n| P02 — Complete the bounded Apple case preparation | running |  |\\\\\\\\n| P03 — Implement source lowering and shared IR | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P04 — Implement reconstruction and numerical operations | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P05 — Execute the bounded company path | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P06 — Enforce context, chronology and resolution | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P07 — Implement review, persistence and recovery | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P08 — Resolve authority and corporate-method obligations | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P09 — Extend bank methods | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P10 — Extend insurance methods | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P11 — Exercise adapters and matched frontends | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P12 — Prepare and exercise a bounded benchmark | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P13 — Develop calibrated forecasting methods and evidence | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n| P14 — Integrate the design and independent-review preparation | pending |  |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Latest outcome\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"accepted_internal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"issues\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [],\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"residuals\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Publication/version evidence, semantic annotation, incorporated packages and benchmark labels remain open.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  ]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Next action\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReview the next eligible slice against these actual outcomes; all gap closures require separate requirement evidence.\\\\\\\\n# Active checkpoint\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\\\\\\\\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\\\\\\\\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\\\\\\\\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\\\\\\\\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\\\\\\\\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\\\\\\\\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\\\\\\\\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\\\\\\\\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\\\\\\\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\\\\\\\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\\\\\\\\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\\\\\\\\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\\\\\\\\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\\\\\\\\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\\\\\\\\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\\\\\\\\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\\\\\\\\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\\\\\\\\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\\\\\\\\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\\\\\\\\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\\\\\\\\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\\\\\\\\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\\\\\\\\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\\\\\\\\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\\\\\\\\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\\\\\\\\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\\\\\\\\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\\\\\\\\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\\\\\\\\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\\\\\\\\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\\\\\\\\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Current deliverable\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf` and its LaTeX sources are Version\\\\\\\\n1.2, a 79-page design candidate with 11 chapters and two appendices. It contains\\\\\\\\ncomplete Northstar annual/interim/revision/forecast cases, an Apple filing\\\\\\\\ninventory and conditional financing stress, historical construction and solver\\\\\\\\nlimits, corporate operations, sector examples, Core 0 contracts,\\\\\\\\nreview/replay/adapter definitions and corpus/release protocols.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe 8 mission goals and MC01–MC34 retain their requirement and acceptance\\\\\\\\nwording. MC35 adds the new cost/preparation requirement. Assessments identify\\\\\\\\nevidence and residual obligations. A bounded debt semantic validator, frozen\\\\\\\\nregistry and three accounting source dossiers supplement the design. Version\\\\\\\\n1.2 corrects the Caterpillar note anchor and states separate reinsurance PAA\\\\\\\\neligibility/recognition/timing; it preserves the prior calculations.\\\\\\\\nControl files:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `MISSION_CONTROL.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/plans/accounting-before-paid-review.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-results.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-manifest.json`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/plans/accounting-gap-repair-2026-10-02.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/repair-plan-review-2026-10-02.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/author-review.md`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/repair-verification.json`\\\\\\\\n- `docs/design/review/repair-execution-note.md`\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe preparation manifest records the earlier Version 1.2 preparation state.\\\\\\\\nCorpus-era controls and `fixtures/corpus-protocol.json` have since been updated;\\\\\\\\ntheir current hashes are in `data/financial-report-benchmark/release-manifest.json`.\\\\\\\\nThe older repair manifest identifies historical Version 1.1; neither historical\\\\\\\\nmanifest should be treated as a current hash set for changed control files.\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/README.md` gives reading routes and commands.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Evidence preserved\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe protected original 60-page draft, controls and affected scripts are under\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/`, with 45 file hashes. Its PDF hash is\\\\\\\\n`0b83e17e8f7906c8ea341cb6c1ef2b3082069ca59577eb0ae7d22b50c54163f0`.\\\\\\\\nVersion 1.1 also remains protected in `pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/`\\\\\\\\n(44 files), with its rendered evidence in `repair-render/version-1.1/`.\\\\\\\\nNo old display equations or citation keys were removed; grammar/record changes\\\\\\\\nand preserved qualifications have an author disposition.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nChecks: 12 original illustrations, 49 repair/reference checks and 31\\\\\\\\ncore-contract/reference checks pass. The new semantic suite passes 78 checks\\\\\\\\n(5 positive, 71 schema-valid negative, 2 JSON-boundary); the new accounting\\\\\\\\ndossiers pass 17 exact/journal checks. These are bounded author evidence. The revised PDF has no serious TeX\\\\\\\\nwarnings and received contact-sheet plus selected full-page inspection.\\\\\\\\nThe verifier requires an author-review file and matching current-PDF render\\\\\\\\nmanifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\\\\\\\\nverified paper PDFs. There are 179 individual title/metadata decisions across\\\\\\\\n194 occurrences and 72 forward queries; missing decisions stop generation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFixtures, grammar, schema and contracts are in `docs/design/fixtures` and\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/spec`. The complete demo IR is author-entered, not generated by a\\\\\\\\ncompiler. The new `core_semantics.py` validates the authored monetary debt\\\\\\\\nprofile and its 17 frozen exports; unsupported sections/operations are rejected.\\\\\\\\nIt does not prove family coverage or execute a general model. Checks evaluate\\\\\\\\nselected IR expressions and reference financial operations; they do not certify\\\\\\\\na production engine.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSelected rule support comes from official AASB texts incorporating IAS 2,\\\\\\\\nIAS 32 and IFRS 17. Mack's chain-ladder technical method, proofs and aggregate\\\\\\\\nerror discussion were inspected. Sources and limits are recorded in\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/research/standards-support.json` and\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Remaining work and next justified steps\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Extend the checked debt-profile registry/reference/type validation and implement source-to-IR lowering\\\\\\\\n   against the positive/negative cases. Schema parsing is not complete compiler\\\\\\\\n   conformance. Preserve assumptions, context, joint symbols and branch failures.\\\\\\\\n2. Build the bounded Northstar path and transactional replay; execute small\\\\\\\\n   version-pinned Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger exchanges as selected.\\\\\\\\n   Only Z3 has been exercised in this repair.\\\\\\\\n3. Expand and independently annotate the real corpus. Apple's 121 annual pages\\\\\\\\n   and 23 total notes are inventoried, but full semantics and incorporated\\\\\\\\n   external documents are incomplete.\\\\\\\\n4. Obtain full ASC authority and official/current ASBE verification. Extend\\\\\\\\n   bank credit/prudential, insurance measurement/transition and richer hybrids\\\\\\\\n   with primary support and complete actual fact patterns. Existing bank capital\\\\\\\\n   assumptions are illustrative, not Basel rules. Dossiers retain source-version\\\\\\\\n   limits and calculations; source acquisition remains internal work.\\\\\\\\n5. After relevant internal tasks are complete, identify any consequential\\\\\\\\n   residual questions for independent implementability/accounting review. Use\\\\\\\\n   the unsent brief with narrow questions and a user-approved scope/cost only\\\\\\\\n   if later commissioned. Ordinary comprehension feedback is separate and need\\\\\\\\n   not come from a professional firm. Acceptance stays provisional while\\\\\\\\n   internal work continues. Forecast calibration, stochastic inference and\\\\\\\\n   performance comparisons need separate evidence plans; none was run here.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nG1–G18 are mapped in the result note; the wider audit is not fully closed.\\\\\\\\nA bounded complete synthetic case must not narrow the mission. No deployment,\\\\\\\\nexternal messaging, Git initialization or production claims were part of this\\\\\\\\nwork. No subagents were used.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Recovery history\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOriginal saved session: `01a0f8e0-0c0b-7332-8f7e-d6b93ce32761`. It failed at\\\\\\\\n06:13:01 after repeated HTTP 502 responses from its model-provider gateway;\\\\\\\\nlogged context-limit flags were false. Last saved prior work was rendered\\\\\\\\ncontact-sheet inspection; its final author-review record was absent. This\\\\\\\\ncampaign supplies a new author review rather than attributing one to that\\\\\\\\ninterrupted session. The upstream gateway cause remains unknown.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOriginal evidence remains in\\\\\\\\n`docs/plans/accounting-product-design-session-recovery.md` and\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/review/session-recovery-2026-10-02/`. Do not restart the literature\\\\\\\\ncollection, initial draft or investigation from scratch. Existing `.git` is not\\\\\\\\na usable repository; do not initialise it or invent a commit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,210p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,180p' scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json; rg -n 'Apple|apple|reconcil|round|history|publication' scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,210p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,180p' scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json; rg -n 'Apple|apple|reconcil|round|history|publication' scripts/check_accounting_dossiers.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# AccDSL mission requirements and acceptance evidence\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEstablished 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong).\\\\\\\\nAuthority: [mission control](../../MISSION_CONTROL.md).\\\\\\\\nScope: requirements for the governing design and the eventual product it\\\\\\\\nspecifies. Current assessments concern the document, not implemented software.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Provenance and assessment rules\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **U1:** original user request on heterogeneous annual/interim reports, all\\\\\\\\n  footnotes, accounting standards, industries, company labels, time, financial\\\\\\\\n  institutions, bonds and equities; saved-session record 10.\\\\\\\\n- **U2:** explicit request to preserve different possible journals,\\\\\\\\n  interpretations and scenario-dependent future distributions; record 115.\\\\\\\\n- **U3:** explicit request for a detailed governing LaTeX design, broad\\\\\\\\n  literature collection, open-source survey, concrete methods, DSL comparison\\\\\\\\n  and adherence to the user's policies; record 145.\\\\\\\\n- **U4:** user direction of 2 October 2026 to complete feasible internal work\\\\\\\\n  before expensive professional review; preserve this work order as MC35.\\\\\\\\n- **U5:** subsequent user direction to build a quarterly/semi-annual benchmark\\\\\\\\n  corpus across regions, industries and standards over preferably 5–10 years\\\\\\\\n  first. The active corpus plan targets eight years and requires five complete\\\\\\\\n  consecutive years per selected issuer; nine issuers are a derived panel choice.\\\\\\\\n- **P:** applicable scientific coding, literature and prose policies.\\\\\\\\n- **D:** a derived engineering/scientific requirement needed to make U1–U3\\\\\\\\n  concrete. It does not make the particular proposed implementation immutable.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe user authorised mission installation and then the reviewed repair plan.\\\\\\\\nAssessments below include the 2 October 2026 repair and subsequent internal\\\\\\\\npreparation; the protected pre-repair\\\\\\\\nregister remains under `docs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/`.\\\\\\\\nThis register continues to control the work.\\\\\\\\nIt does not retrospectively approve every technical choice in the manuscript.\\\\\\\\nTraceability uses MC IDs to avoid confusing this register with the manuscript's\\\\\\\\nolder R1–R10 summary. M1–M8 are goals in the root mission document. G1–G10 refer\\\\\\\\nto the [initial gap audit](../design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md); G11–G18 refer\\\\\\\\nto the [expanded audit](../design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`Partial` means the draft addresses the topic but its required design evidence\\\\\\\\nis incomplete. `Open` means the essential concrete deliverable is still absent.\\\\\\\\n`Specified` and `Checked` require explicit evidence and scope. An implemented\\\\\\\\nfeature, accounting-valid treatment and empirically supported forecast each\\\\\\\\nneed their own evidence; no design status implies any of them. The acceptance\\\\\\\\ncolumn defines the unchanged obligation; the assessment records the evidence\\\\\\\\nactually supplied. Chapter numbers refer to the revised PDF. The [repair result\\\\\\\\nmap](../design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md) links the supporting files\\\\\\\\nand outstanding work. A reference check is a bounded design oracle, not a\\\\\\\\nproduction conformance test. The supplemental [preparation results](../design/review/internal-preparation-results.md)\\\\\\\\nrecord bounded implementation evidence separately from the design and professional acceptance.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M1 — Historical record and meaning\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\\\\\\\\n| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\\\\\\\\n| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\\\\\\\\n| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\\\\\\\\n| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\\\\\\\\n| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\\\\\\\\n| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\\\\\\\\n| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\\\\\\\\n| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\\\\\\\\n| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\\\\\\\\n| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\\\\\\\\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\\\\\\\\n| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\\\\\\\\n| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\\\\\\\n| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\\\\\\\\n| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\\\\\\\\n| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\\\\\\\\n| MC21 | Represent banks' liabilities, assets, deposits, capital and regulatory/economic constraints. U1, U2. | Define core bank structural records now and operation-level later methods for funding, credit, liquidity and capital, including accounting/prudential reconciliation and an appropriate worked case. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 specifies bank origination, transfer, interest, allowance, cash funding and default; exact fixture balances and capital reconciliation pass. Prudential weights are illustrative; full allowance lifecycle, IFRS 9/CECL and jurisdictional capital rules remain open. G7, G8. |\\\\\\\\n| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M5 — Concrete methods, DSL and implementation contracts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\\\\\\\\n| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\\\\\\\\n| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\\\\\\\\n| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\\\\\\\\n| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\\\\\\\\n| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M6 — Literature, sources and reusable software\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\\\\\\\\n| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\\\\\\\\n| MC31 | Survey open-source tools and define evidence-based reuse boundaries. U3, P, D. | Inspect official interfaces/licences, identify supported subsets, specify adapter exchanges and version assumptions, and separate inspected capabilities from later integration/performance evidence. | Inspected software snapshots/licences retained; Ch. 10/Core 0 specify typed exchanges, errors and concrete examples. Z3 is exercised. Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger integrations and pinned deployment combinations remain pending. G9. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M7 — Governing scholarly design\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## M8 — Validation, completion and sustained direction\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| MC33 | Define meaningful acceptance and separate engineering, accounting and scientific evidence. U3, P, D. | Provide canonical conformance inputs/outputs, corpus/annotation rules, justified release-specific criteria, review status and later forecast baselines/uncertainty protocols. Existing arithmetic/build checks keep their limited meanings. | Specified fixtures, corpus strata, annotation/adjudication/split protocol, hard conformance vetoes and provisional workload limits in Ch. 11/`corpus-protocol.json`. Reference checks, new debt semantic rejection cases, accounting dossiers and author review recorded; the 192-report source panel now passes acquisition acceptance and independent integrity checks. Annotation protocol/schema and provisional family roles exist; adjudication, performance and release validation remain pending. G5, G10. |\\\\\\\\n| MC34 | Stage implementation without losing the full mission or concealing unresolved decisions. U1, U2, U3, P, D. | Maintain requirement-to-section/case/gap traceability, explicit current-versus-later support, dependency order, workload assumptions and open decisions. Re-audit after material changes and test interactions, not just individual rows. | Original 34 requirement/acceptance pairs preserved; assessments updated and MC35 added from U4. The reviewed repair plan and G1–G18 result map preserve current/later/source-blocked obligations; implementation order remains in Ch. 11. Wider mission and acceptance stay active. G1–G18. |\\\\\\\\n| MC35 | Complete feasible internal preparation before paid professional review and minimise avoidable reviewer effort. U4. | Allocate every residual gap to internal work or a specific professional judgment; supply checked facts, dated sources, a proposed answer, counterargument and consequences before referral. Any later engagement has explicit user authority and an agreed bounded scope/cost. Keep human acceptance separate from continued internal work. | Standing rule installed in mission/AGENTS. All G1–G18 allocated in `review/internal-before-expert.md`; debt semantic checks, three source dossiers, journal checks and manuscript corrections completed. The review brief is unsent; actual-company facts, source and implementation tasks remain internal. No paid-review readiness, spending authority or savings estimate is claimed. The eight-year corpus, provenance checks, 20 regression tests and annotation preparation format were completed internally without professional engagement. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Current disposition and maintenance\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe local repair campaign supplied concrete methods, cases, contracts and\\\\\\\\nreference evidence; it did not complete the wider product mission. The\\\\\\\\n[repair results](../design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md) distinguish\\\\\\\\nspecified behaviour, checked examples, source limitations and later execution.\\\\\\\\nHuman comprehension, independent accounting and implementation review remain\\\\\\\\npending. Complete all feasible dependent internal work before paid review;\\\\\\\\nthese statuses do not prevent further authorised internal work. Ordinary reader\\\\\\\\nfeedback does not require an accounting-firm engagement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nU5 source acquisition is accepted: active panel v2 contains all 192 target\\\\\\\\nreports, with eight consecutive complete years for each of nine issuers.\\\\\\\\nHenkel and Munich Re replace two inaccessible interim series under the reviewed\\\\\\\\nplan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\\\\\\\\nMC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\\\\\\\\nrequirements. The [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\\\\\\\\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/coverage.json` and matching independent\\\\\\\\n`integrity-manifest.json` preserve acceptance. Filing dates are evidenced for\\\\\\\\n56 reports; 136 publication dates remain unverified. Counts are not accuracy scores.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFollowing source acceptance, extend the checked authored-debt semantics/registry to the remaining\\\\\\\\nCore 0 profile and shared-IR compiler, then implement the bounded Northstar path and\\\\\\\\nselected adapters. In parallel with later domain design, acquire missing\\\\\\\\nprimary authority, expand the real corpus and resolve substantive annotation\\\\\\\\nquestions. Richer bank/insurance and continuous inference methods retain their\\\\\\\\nseparate milestones; the bounded core does not redefine those requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUpdate affected rows after substantive changes. Preserve the requirement and\\\\\\\\nacceptance wording unless the user changes scope. New findings may be added;\\\\\\\\nthese 35 requirements and 18 gap categories are a traceable baseline, not a\\\\\\\\nproof that no further omissions can be found.\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"schema_version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"accdsl.master.catalog.v1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"date\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-10-02\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mission\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MISSION_CONTROL.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gap_register\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"limits\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phase_seconds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 900,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"review_seconds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 240,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"plan_seconds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 240,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"max_repairs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run_seconds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 7200\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"phases\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P00\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"builtin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Verify the accepted baseline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gaps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G18\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC30\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC33\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC34\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC35\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"objective\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Verify the frozen source release and rerun the existing bounded engineering/reference checks without replacing their historical output files.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"baseline.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Frozen release input hashes still match; independent corpus verification passes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Existing bounded suites run successfully; their scopes are preserved.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No manuscript, source corpus or historical release evidence is overwritten.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ]\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"builtin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prepare source-context and availability work records\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P00\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gaps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G11\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G13\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC02\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC05\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC33\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"objective\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Create one source-grounded work record for each accepted report, preserving version identity, basis evidence, source locations and unresolved availability/package/semantic obligations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source-work-register.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exactly the accepted report IDs occur once, with original and extraction hashes verified.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sourced filing dates remain distinct from unknown publication and byte-vintage evidence.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No record is promoted to a gold accounting label or complete disclosure package.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ]\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P02\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Complete the bounded Apple case preparation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gaps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G11\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G13\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC03\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC05\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC16\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC28\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"objective\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Build a source-anchored annual/interim Apple case layer over the existing retained files: every inventoried note has an explicit modelling disposition, selected statement/note bridges are machine-checked, external incorporations remain visible, and known unidentified histories are preserved. Implement reusable extraction/context/reconciliation code rather than copying authored conclusions.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"case.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"result.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"All 13 annual and 10 interim notes have source anchors, linked quantities or explicit unresolved meaning, with no claim that dispositions alone close semantics.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Reconciliation uses source-bound values and exact rounding-aware expectations; wrong scale/sign/perimeter and broken source anchors are rejected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Incorporated proxy/agreement and publication-version obligations are investigated using legitimate public sources where available, and unresolved obligations are specific.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Tests include real retained input and independent arithmetic/source checks; no full-company forecast is claimed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tests/test_accounting_p02.py\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"output_dir\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P03\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"worker\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Implement source lowering and shared IR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P00\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gaps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"G15\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC02\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC04\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC20\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC23\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MC24\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"objective\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Implement executable DSL source-to-IR lowering and an equivalent typed-library entrypoint for the declared Core 0 supported profile. Start with borrowing.acc and expand beyond an exact fixture lookup. Preserve package bindings, source context, assumptions and alternatives. Never label a JSON/schema parser as a semantic compiler.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deliverables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"conformance.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"result.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"criteria\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Actual source programs lower through parsing, binding, package/type/context checks into validated shared IR.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Equivalent typed-library programs have matching semantics and changed valid inputs produce changed results rather than returning a frozen fixture.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Independent source variants and schema-valid negative programs test