ntextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-65-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-66-Equivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-67-concepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-68-conditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-69-case showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-70-or two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-71-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-72-Required evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-73-similar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-74-quantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\\\\\\\\n--\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-80-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-81-Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-82-Evidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-83-and [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-84-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-85-Storing dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-86-query. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-87-conflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-88-bases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-89-queries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-90-delegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-91-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-92-Required evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-93-economic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\\\\\\\\n--\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-125-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-126-Evidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-127-and [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-128-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-129-Sales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-130-recognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-131-reference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-132-settlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-133-and changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-134-restatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-135-specifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-136-properties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-137-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-138-Required repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\\\\\\\\n--\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-146-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-147-Evidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-148-[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-149-and [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-150-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-151-The document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-152-instantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-153-set with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-154-cross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-155-The mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-156-has already been supplied by hand.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-157-\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-158-Required repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md-159-and a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\\\\\\\\nglobal-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md\\\\\\\\nhumanizer-ai-writing-patterns.md\\\\\\\\nscholarly-literature-audit-policy.md\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_11\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The existing Apple builder hard-codes selected statement amounts; P02 needs extraction and validation against the retained sources. P01’s register is under the accepted run directory, not `deliverables/P01`. I’ll use that register and preserve the existing manifests.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_12\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,160p' /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md; sed -n '39,102p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '124,166p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_12\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,160p' /home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies/global-scientific-coding-agent-policy.md; sed -n '39,102p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '124,166p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Global Scientific Coding Agent Policy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis policy is intended for all projects where an agent writes code, runs\\\\\\\\nexperiments, interprets numerical results, or helps with scientific documents.\\\\\\\\nIt is project-independent. Project-local `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` files may\\\\\\\\nadd stricter rules for a specific repository.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Context, Tool Output, And Recovery Discipline\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Keep the active question, current stage, checked findings, evidence paths,\\\\\\\\n  remaining execution budget, and exact next action in one concise checkpoint.\\\\\\\\n  Replace completed-task instructions with the next task; keep detailed history\\\\\\\\n  in linked result files instead of expanding the checkpoint indefinitely.\\\\\\\\n- Read only the source ranges and structured-result fields needed for the next\\\\\\\\n  decision. Normally return at most about 2,000 tokens per tool response and\\\\\\\\n  4,000 per combined batch. Per-command budgets add up: bound the outer tool\\\\\\\\n  response too. These are context budgets, not limits on scientific rigor.\\\\\\\\n- Search for file names or counts first, then inspect selected matching lines.\\\\\\\\n  When output is truncated, narrow the query or read another exact range;\\\\\\\\n  do not automatically increase the output allowance or repeat a broad dump.\\\\\\\\n- Preserve complete command logs on disk and return exit status, key findings,\\\\\\\\n  and artifact paths. Do not print entire nested tool results or recursively\\\\\\\\n  reproduce old outputs. Parse only the exact saved session and selected fields\\\\\\\\n  when investigating an incident; never dump raw session JSONL or instruction\\\\\\\\n  payloads into the active research conversation.\\\\\\\\n- Use explicit working directories and cross-checkout paths. Save findings\\\\\\\\n  after each substantive result and before a large operation. Checkpoint well\\\\\\\\n  before the configured compaction threshold; no universal threshold or output\\\\\\\\n  setting proves that a model provider can complete compaction.\\\\\\\\n- While compaction is unreliable, use fresh research conversations at completed\\\\\\\\n  stage boundaries, initialized from the concise checkpoint and governing\\\\\\\\n  instructions. Keep incident investigation separate. Resuming or forking a\\\\\\\\n  failed conversation can retain its oversized history. Continue authorized\\\\\\\\n  work within a healthy stage; this rule creates no new approval gate and does\\\\\\\\n  not authorize launching another agent without the applicable authorization.\\\\\\\\n- After repeated pre-turn compaction failures, preserve the failed session and\\\\\\\\n  recover from the checkpoint. Do not inflate the declared context window,\\\\\\\\n  remove applicable instructions, or disable safeguards to force old history\\\\\\\\n  through. Tool-output discipline reduces pressure; provider faults require\\\\\\\\n  separate diagnosis. Distinguish character counts, active-context token counts,\\\\\\\\n  and cumulative billing counts in incident reports.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Post-Compaction Verification Protocol\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Treat a compaction summary as a memory aid. The user's current directive and\\\\\\\\n  earlier authorization remain authoritative; a new steering message normally\\\\\\\\n  refines the active task rather than replacing it.\\\\\\\\n- Before modifying files or resuming an experiment, verify the checkout, branch,\\\\\\\\n  relevant working-tree changes, and concise active checkpoint. Read exact plan\\\\\\\\n  sections only as needed; do not reload every master plan, incident report, or\\\\\\\\n  unrelated dirty file to reconstruct context.\\\\\\\\n- Confirm that the next action answers the active question and respects the\\\\\\\\n  existing scope, evidence contract, and remaining budget. Preserve unrelated\\\\\\\\n  edits. Resolve routine ambiguity from current user messages and saved evidence;\\\\\\\\n  ask only if a material unresolved choice affects correctness, permissions,\\\\\\\\n  cost, privacy, irreversible state, publication, or project direction.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Academic Research Governance And Proportionality\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- For trusted local academic and research repositories, optimize governance for\\\\\\\\n  scientific validity, reproducibility, bounded compute, and progress. Do not\\\\\\\\n  import production-service security ceremony without a concrete applicable\\\\\\\\n  threat.\\\\\\\\n- Distinguish scientific rigor from operational security. Evidence contracts,\\\\\\\\n  mathematical checks, statistical uncertainty, source grounding, exact run\\\\\\\\n  manifests, and honest nonclaims remain strict. Launch-token mechanics do not\\\\\\\\n  become scientific evidence merely because they are elaborate.\\\\\\\\n- The default local threat model is accidental error in a trusted workspace,\\\\\\\\n  not a hostile multi-tenant service. Git provenance, unique versioned output\\\\\\\\n  directories, ordinary checksums, focused tests, run manifests, and preserved\\\\\\\\n  prior results are normally sufficient for research integrity.\\\\\\\\n- Unless a plan identifies a concrete adversarial risk or the user explicitly\\\\\\\\n  requests stronger controls, do not require:\\\\\\\\n  - hash-bound natural-language approval statements;\\\\\\\\n  - one-use authority, approval-token, or permanent launch-claim files;\\\\\\\\n  - inode, descriptor, hard-link, immutable-empty-file, or crash-durable output\\\\\\\\n    reservation protocols;\\\\\\\\n  - custom cryptographic schemas when Git and ordinary SHA-256 artifacts answer\\\\\\\\n    the integrity question;\\\\\\\\n  - separate human approval for each local retry under an unchanged scientific\\\\\\\\n    contract and campaign budget; or\\\\\\\\n  - mandatory review of every proposal, manifest, subplan, result, and handoff.\\\\\\\\n- Extra security machinery is justified only when the artifact states the\\\\\\\\n  threat, why normal academic controls are insufficient, and why the mechanism\\\\\\\\n  is proportionate. Security complexity without that analysis is a governance\\\\\\\\n  defect and should be removed, not expanded.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Execution Tiers\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Routine local work:** implementation, unit tests, focused diagnostics,\\\\\\\\n  import/compile checks, and short smokes need no special governance approval\\\\\\\\n  beyond the user's task and normal tool permissions.\\\\\\\\n- **Serious local research campaign:** long experiments, MCMC/ML runs,\\\\\\\\n  benchmark ladders, and research-decision runs need one concise experiment\\\\\\\\n  plan with an evidence contract, total compute/attempt budget, versioned output\\\\\\\\n  root, and stop conditions. A plain-language user request to execute or resume\\\\\\\\n  the plan is sufficient campaign authorization. No magic wording or manifest\\\\\\\\n  hash is required.\\\\\\\\n- **External or irreversible work:** require explicit human approval at the\\\\\\\\n  actual boundary for public release or messaging, credentials/secrets,\\\\\\\\n  destructive operations, broad package/environment mutation, paid or\\\\\\\\n  materially expanded compute, privacy-boundary changes, or material\\\\\\\\n  scientific/product-direction changes.\\\\\\\\n- Platform, sandbox, and tool permission requirements still apply. This policy\\\\\\\\n  removes self-imposed ceremony; it does not bypass controls the agent does not\\\\\\\\n  own.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Campaign Repair And Retry\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Within an authorized serious campaign, repair and retry a localized\\\\\\\\n  infrastructure, harness, serialization, multiprocessing, or resource failure\\\\\\\\n  without renewed approval when the target, data, method, promotion criteria,\\\\\\\\n  vetoes, hardware class, privacy boundary, and total campaign budget remain\\\\\\\\n  unchanged.\\\\\\\\n- Record each attempt, failure classification, repair, focused regression, wall\\\\\\\\n  time, and remaining budget. Use a fresh versioned output directory for every\\\\\\\\n  launch and never overwrite prior evidence.\\\\\\\\n- A failed candidate or infrastructure attempt consumes campaign budget, not a\\\\\\\\n  magic authority token. Stop for new direction only when the scientific\\\\\\\\n  contract or budget changes, a true continuation veto fires, or the campaign\\\\\\\\n  budget is exhausted.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Review Proportionality\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Review is advisory by default, not execution authority. Use independent\\\\\\\\n  review when it materially reduces scientific or engineering risk, especially\\\\\\\\n  for source-faithfulness, publication-grade claims, major public API/default\\\\\\\\n  changes, unusually expensive campaigns, or user-requested review.\\\\\\\\n- One material plan review and one terminal result review are normally enough\\\\\\\\n  for a serious campaign. Routine work and localized infrastructure repairs do\\\\\\\\n  not require a review chain when focused checks answer the risk.\\\\\\\\n- Reviewer unavailability, timeout, or disagreement about purely procedural\\\\\\\\n  formatting must not block trusted local research when the scientific plan,\\\\\\\\n  focused checks, artifacts, and budget are adequate. Record the limitation and\\\\\\\\n  continue. A material scientific, numerical, privacy, cost, or destructive-\\\\\\\\n  action finding remains a real blocker.\\\\\\\\n- Do not create review packets and governance artifacts whose only purpose is\\\\\\\\n  to authorize more review packets and governance artifacts.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Legacy Governance Migration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- The newest applicable `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` policy governs active work.\\\\\\\\n  When it retires older procedural ceremony, preserve old artifacts as\\\\\\\\n  historical evidence but do not finish, regenerate, or satisfy superseded\\\\\\\\n  approval-token and manifest gates.\\\\\\\\n- Write a short migration note and a concise active campaign plan. Do not make\\\\\\\\n  the simplification itself pass through the retired ceremony.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Codex Session Route Recovery\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWhen an approval, gateway, or session route is disputed, run the installed\\\\\\\\nread-only checker at ~/.codex/bin/codex-route-doctor --json and read the\\\\\\\\nrunbook at ~/.local/share/claudecodex/codex-session-recovery.md. A local allow\\\\\\\\nresult does not override a managed reviewer, and a pre-process\\\\\\\\ngpt-5.6-luna HTTP 404 is a managed-reviewer/session issue rather than evidence\\\\\\\\nthat the code, GPU, or scientific method is impossible. If the shared runbook\\\\\\\\nis inaccessible, retain those two distinctions and report the exact failing\\\\\\\\nlayer before proposing a gateway change.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Working Style\\\\\\\\n### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [source coverage](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:6)\\\\\\\\nand [narrative assertions](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:44).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe draft requires dispositions for source spans and separates document,\\\\\\\\nsemantic and simulation coverage. It does not specify how to establish the\\\\\\\\ncomplete disclosure inventory, resolve incorporated cross-references, carry\\\\\\\\nqualifications from narrative into the affected figures, or verify that the\\\\\\\\ncoverage process itself has not missed a note or table. Generic actor/predicate\\\\\\\\nfields are insufficient to determine the executable meaning of exclusions,\\\\\\\\nscope qualifications, contingent commitments and qualitative quantifiers.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired evidence: one complete filing manifest, source-span disposition and\\\\\\\\ncross-reference example; typed narrative records; a mapping from disclosures\\\\\\\\nto supported constraints or explicit unresolved obligations. Preserve separate\\\\\\\\ncoverage meanings and defined denominators. Do not score parsed pages as\\\\\\\\nformalised financial meaning, or turn \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"substantially all\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" into an invented\\\\\\\\nnumeric threshold.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\\\\\\\\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\\\\\\\\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\\\\\\\\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\\\\\\\\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\\\\\\\\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\\\\\\\\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\\\\\\\\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\\\\\\\\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\\\\\\\\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\\\\\\\\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\\\\\\\\nand [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStoring dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\\\\\\\\nquery. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\\\\\\\\nconflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\\\\\\\\nbases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\\\\\\\\nqueries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\\\\\\\\ndelegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\\\\\\\\neconomic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\\\\\\\\nrecords/results returned by each supported view. Show invalid year-to-date\\\\\\\\nsubtractions across revisions as well as a valid one. Declare unsupported\\\\\\\\ntiming assumptions rather than silently using the latest available row.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [three scenario meanings](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/03-literature.tex:149),\\\\\\\\n[information timing](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:121),\\\\\\\\n### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\\\\\\\\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\\\\\\\\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\\\\\\\\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\\\\\\\\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\\\\\\\\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\\\\\\\\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\\\\\\\\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\\\\\\\\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\\\\\\\\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\\\\\\\\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\\\\\\\\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\\\\\\\\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\\\\\\\\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\\\\\\\\n[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\\\\\\\\nand [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\\\\\\\\ninstantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\\\\\\\\nset with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\\\\\\\\ncross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\\\\\\\\nThe mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\\\\\\\\nhas already been supplied by hand.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRequired repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\\\\\\\\nand a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\\\\\\\\nnotes including narrative qualifications, missing terms, a contradiction and\\\\\\\\na revised comparative. A worked specification can be written before the\\\\\\\\nengine exists; the gap is not simply the absence of production code.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEvidence: [forward equations](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:119),\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n '97,341|96,662|94,804|14,575|88.4|Note 9|Note 6|incorporat|2025 Proxy|Credit Agreement|364,980|391,035|124,300' docs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt | head -95; sed -n '1,100p' scripts/core_semantics.py; rg --files docs/design | rg 'apple|temporal|history|real|debt'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_13\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n '97,341|96,662|94,804|14,575|88.4|Note 9|Note 6|incorporat|2025 Proxy|Credit Agreement|364,980|391,035|124,300' docs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt | head -95; sed -n '1,100p' scripts/core_semantics.py; rg --files docs/design | rg 'apple|temporal|history|real|debt'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:509:of incorporation or organization)\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:645:124,300\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:819:364,980\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:889:364,980\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1186:124,300\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1643:14,575\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1645:14,575\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1732:Note 6 –\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1750:88.4\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1827:Note 9 –\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1931:The Company periodically provides certain information for investors on its corporate website, www.apple.com, and its investor relations website, investor.apple.com. This includes press releases and other information about financial performance, information on environmental, social and governance matters, and details related to the Company’s annual meeting of shareholders. The information contained on the websites referenced in this Form 10-Q is not incorporated by reference into this filing. Further, the Company’s references to website URLs are intended to be inactive textual references only.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:1987:124,300\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt:2040:124,300\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:24:                         of incorporation or organization)\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:95:Portions of the Registrant’s definitive proxy statement relating to its 2025 annual meeting of shareholders are incorporated by reference into Part III of this Annual Report on Form\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:356:information contained on the websites referenced in this Form 10-K is not incorporated by reference into this filing. Further, the Company’s references to website\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:638:content, as well as the right to incorporate specific content into the Company’s own services. The licensing or other distribution arrangements for this content can\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1202:    Total net sales                                             $        391,035                     2% $       383,285               (3)% $          394,328\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1239:       Total net sales                                                      $         391,035                    2% $              383,285        (3)% $     394,328\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1503:    Total net sales                                                                                           391,035               383,285               394,328\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1590:             Total assets                                                                                             $           364,980   $           352,583\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1615:               Total liabilities and shareholders’ equity                                                             $           364,980 $             352,583\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1824:     Total net sales                                                                                          $            391,035    $     383,285   $          394,328\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1972:    Interest rate contracts                                                                                      $              14,575   $              19,375\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2018:Note 6 – Consolidated Financial Statement Details\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2218:\\\\\\\\fNote 9 – Debt\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2247:    Fixed-rate 0.000% – 4.850% notes                           2024 – 2062       $           97,341             0.03% – 6.65%       $         106,572             0.03% – 6.72%\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2248:         Total term debt principal                                                           97,341                                           106,572\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2252:         Total term debt                                                                     96,662                                           105,103\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2272:    Total term debt principal                                                                                                                              $                 97,341\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2278:\\\\\\\\fAs of September 28, 2024 and September 30, 2023, the fair value of the Company’s Notes, based on Level 2 inputs, was $88.4 billion and $90.8 billion,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2458:         Total net sales                                                                                  $         391,035      $           383,285       $      394,328\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2687:September 28, 2024, in connection with the solicitation of proxies for the Company’s 2025 annual meeting of shareholders (the “2025 Proxy Statement”), and is\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2688:incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2693:The information required by this Item will be included in the 2025 Proxy Statement, and is incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2698:The information required by this Item will be included in the 2025 Proxy Statement, and is incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2703:The information required by this Item will be included in the 2025 Proxy Statement, and is incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:2708:The information required by this Item will be included in the 2025 Proxy Statement, and is incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3372:company, trust, unincorporated organization or government or any agency or political subdivision thereof or any other entity.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3689:Employee Stock Plan and the Terms and Conditions of Restricted Stock Unit Award, which are incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3701:award (the “Award”) granted by Apple Inc., a California corporation (the “Company”), and are incorporated by reference in the Notice of Grant\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3909:provisions of the Plan, incorporated herein by reference. The Participant agrees to be bound by the terms of the Plan and this Award Agreement.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3994:incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4008:restricted stock unit award (the “Award”) granted by Apple Inc., a California corporation (the “Company”), and are incorporated by reference in\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4014:Terms (including Exhibit A hereto, incorporated herein by this reference) are collectively referred to as the “Award Agreement” applicable to the\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4218:provisions of the Plan, incorporated herein by reference. The Participant agrees to be bound by the terms of the Plan and this Award Agreement.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4399:Employee Stock Plan and the Terms and Conditions of Restricted Stock Unit Award, which are incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4411:award (the “Award”) granted by Apple Inc., a California corporation (the “Company”), and are incorporated by reference in the Notice of Grant\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4639:provisions of the Plan, incorporated herein by reference. The Participant agrees to be bound by the terms of the Plan and this Award Agreement.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4723:incorporated herein by reference.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4737:restricted stock unit award (the “Award”) granted by Apple Inc., a California corporation (the “Company”), and are incorporated by reference in\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4743:Terms (including Exhibit A hereto, incorporated herein by this reference) are collectively referred to as the “Award Agreement” applicable to the\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:4949:provisions of the Plan, incorporated herein by reference. The Participant agrees to be bound by the terms of the Plan and this Award Agreement.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:5339:We consent to the incorporation by reference in the following Registration Statements:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bounded semantic validator for the authored debt IR; no general compiler.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRejects unsupported populated sections and operations explicitly. External\\\\\\\\nexports are frozen data, never executable code or network-loaded dependencies.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\\\\\\\\nfrom fractions import Fraction\\\\\\\\nimport hashlib\\\\\\\\nimport json\\\\\\\\nimport re\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport jsonschema\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nfrom build_demo_registry import build as expected_registry, canonical\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nclass Invalid(Exception):\\\\\\\\n    def __init__(self, code, location, detail):\\\\\\\\n        self.code, self.location, self.detail = code, location, detail\\\\\\\\n        super().__init__(f'{code} at {location}: {detail}')\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef require(condition, code, location, detail):\\\\\\\\n    if not condition:\\\\\\\\n        raise Invalid(code, location, detail)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef strict_json(text):\\\\\\\\n    def pairs(items):\\\\\\\\n        out = {}\\\\\\\\n        for key, value in items:\\\\\\\\n            require(key not in out, 'DuplicateJSONKey', key, 'Duplicate keys lose source information')\\\\\\\\n            out[key] = value\\\\\\\\n        return out\\\\\\\\n    def invalid_constant(value):\\\\\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidJSONNumber', value, 'Non-finite numbers are not JSON')\\\\\\\\n    return json.loads(text, object_pairs_hook=pairs, parse_constant=invalid_constant)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef rational(value, location):\\\\\\\\n    n, d = int(value['n']), int(value['d'])\\\\\\\\n    require(d > 0, 'InvalidRational', location, 'Positive denominator required')\\\\\\\\n    q = Fraction(n, d)\\\\\\\\n    require((str(q.numerator), str(q.denominator)) == (value['n'], value['d']),\\\\\\\\n            'NoncanonicalRational', location, 'Use reduced terms and zero 0/1')\\\\\\\\n    return q\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef iso_date(value, location):\\\\\\\\n    try:\\\\\\\\n        result = date.fromisoformat(value)\\\\\\\\n        require(result.isoformat() == value, 'InvalidDate', location, 'Use YYYY-MM-DD')\\\\\\\\n        return result\\\\\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidDate', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef instant(value, location):\\\\\\\\n    try:\\\\\\\\n        t = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\\\\\\\n        require(t.tzinfo is not None, 'MissingTimezone', location, 'Timestamp requires timezone')\\\\\\\\n        return t\\\\\\\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\\\\\\\n        raise Invalid('InvalidTimestamp', location, str(exc)) from exc\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSUPPORTED = {'models', 'contexts', 'sourceSpans', 'documents', 'observations',\\\\\\\\n             'entities', 'books', 'accounts', 'symbols', 'expressions', 'constraints',\\\\\\\\n             'assumptions', 'alternatives', 'contracts', 'states', 'packages',\\\\\\\\n             'scenarios', 'reviewDecisions', 'evidenceViews', 'modelScopes',\\\\\\\\n             'historyFamilies', 'reportMappings'}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nclass Validator:\\\\\\\\n    def __init__(self, document, registry, schema, root):\\\\\\\\n        try:\\\\\\\\n            jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema).validate(document)\\\\\\\\n        except jsonschema.ValidationError as exc:\\\\\\\\n            raise Invalid('StructuralError', '/'.join(map(str, exc.path)), exc.message) from exc\\\\\\\\n        self.doc, self.root, self.nodes, self.kinds = document, root, {}, {}\\\\\\\\n        self.external, self.values, self.inferred = {}, {}, {}\\\\\\\\n        for section, rows in document.items():\\\\\\\\n            if section == 'schema_version':\\\\\\\\n                continue\\\\\\\\n            require(not rows or section in SUPPORTED, 'UnsupportedSection', section,\\\\\\\\n                    'This preparation checker does not validate this populated section')\\\\\\\\n            for row in rows:\\\\\\\\n                identifier = row['id']\\\\\\\\n                require(identifier not in self.nodes, 'DuplicateID', identifier, 'IDs are globally unique')\\\\\\\\n                self.nodes[identifier], self.kinds[identifier] = row, section\\\\\\\\n        expected = {r['id']: r for r in expected_registry()['records']}\\\\\\\\n        require(isinstance(registry, dict) and registry.get('version') == '1' and\\\\\\\\n                registry.get('profile') == 'authored-debt-example' and\\\\\\\\n                isinstance(registry.get('records'), list), 'UnsupportedRegistry', 'registry',\\\\\\\\n                'Expected the versioned authored debt export set')\\\\\\\\n        for row in registry['records']:\\\\\\\\n            require(isinstance(row, dict) and set(row) == {'id', 'kind', 'artifact', 'sha256', 'pointer', 'value'},\\\\\\\\n                    'RegistryShape', 'registry', 'Export has missing or unknown fields')\\\\\\\\n            identifier = row['id']\\\\\\\\n            require(isinstance(identifier, str) and identifier in expected, 'UnsupportedRegistry', str(identifier),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-source-units.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/research/standards/temporal2018.pdf\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.pdf\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.html\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/chapters/02-history.tex\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/research/raw/temporal-search.html\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/research/raw/temporal-author.html\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/scripts/build_real_case.py\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/review/pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/docs/design/fixtures/demo-debt-package.json\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_14\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\