.txt:5406:\\\\f                                                                                                                                                        Exhibit 31.2\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:5445:              (b) Any fraud, whether or not material, that involves management or other employees who have a significant role in the Registrant’s internal\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:5456:\\\\f                                                                                                                                                    Exhibit 32.1\\\\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:5496:\\\\f                                                                                                              Exhibit 97.1\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files --hidden -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '\\\\\\\"'!docs/design/review/pre-*/**'\\\\\\\"' -g '\\\\\\\"'!data/financial-report-benchmark/**'\\\\\\\"' && sed -n '1,100p' AGENTS.md && rg -n 'MC01|MC03|MC05|MC16|MC28' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files --hidden -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '\\\\\\\"'!docs/design/review/pre-*/**'\\\\\\\"' -g '\\\\\\\"'!data/financial-report-benchmark/**'\\\\\\\"' && sed -n '1,100p' AGENTS.md && rg -n 'MC01|MC03|MC05|MC16|MC28' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"AGENTS.md\\\\n# AccDSL project instructions\\\\n\\\\n## Mission entry point\\\\n\\\\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\\\\n\\\\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\\\\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\\\\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\\\\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\\\\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\\\\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\\\\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\\\\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\\\\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\\\\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\\\\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\\\\n\\\\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\\\\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\\\\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\\\\n\\\\n## Working rules\\\\n\\\\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\\\\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\\\\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\\\\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\\\\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\\\\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\\\\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\\\\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\\\\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\\\\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\\\\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\\\\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\\\\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\\\\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\\\\n- Follow the applicable policies under\\\\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\\\\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\\\\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\\\\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\\\\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\\\\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\\\\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\\\\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\\\\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\\\\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\\\\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\\\\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\\\\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\\\\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\\\\n\\\\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\\\\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\\\\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\\\\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\\\\n55:| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\\\\n57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\\\\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\\\\n80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\\\\n102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\\\\n140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\\\\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\\\nimport json\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/source-work-register.json'); d=json.loads(p.read_text()); print('keys',list(d))\\\\ndef wal