{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/result.md && printf '\\\\n--- files ---\\\\n' && find data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02 -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f %s bytes\\\\n' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# P02 execution record\n\nScope: MC01, MC03, MC05, MC16 and MC28 for Apple's retained fiscal 2024\nannual and fiscal 2025 first-quarter disclosures and their comparatives.\nImplementation is in progress; this initial record precedes implementation.\nPlan provenance: approved phase packet, plan hash\n`916a4c80553bebee3ca0b6399ba8d4e54a6f5d3bd2975cda75815b95e8f45f59`.\n\n## Pre-execution skeptical audit and evidence contract\n\nThe reviewed plan passes a fresh audit against the retained inputs. The\nbaseline is the original PDF/HTML and their separately identified extractions,\nnot authored totals in the existing builder. The existing 372-file inventory\nmatches phase entry. Git is unavailable (the existing marker is not a usable\nrepository); it will not be initialized. No controller, benchmark, snapshot or\nexisting case file will be edited.\n\nQuestion: can reusable extraction recover selected typed readings, explicitly\naccount for all 23 notes, and check the declared statement/note bridges?\nPass requires source bindings, supported context, exact arithmetic or explicit\nrounding compatibility, 23 bounded note dispositions, and adversarial rejection\ntests. Hash/anchor failures, missing/duplicate required notes, ambiguous required\nreadings, invalid contexts and failed arithmetic veto the implementation until\nrepaired. External-access failures block only their dependent incorporation or\nversion claims. Counts and reconciliations cannot establish semantic completion,\naccounting compliance, forecast validity or human acceptance.\n\nThe expected failure modes are copied constants, mixed extraction offsets,\nwrong scale/sign/date, cash-perimeter substitution, fair value or notional\nsubstitution for carrying value, and overlapping revenue partitions. These are\nrepair triggers and deterministic test targets. A successful build without these\nchecks would not answer the question. No statistical comparison, research run,\nperformance ranking or numerical default promotion is planned; a tuned baseline\nladder and random seeds are inapplicable. Stop for corrupted required inputs or\nunsupported mandatory extraction; preserve specific external residuals and\ncontinue independent work. Only the two declared files are written under the\nmaster deliverable directory.\n\n| Choice | Provenance and status | Justification / failure mode | Early diagnostic |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PDF layout extraction and BeautifulSoup HTML parsing | Existing available tools; bounded implementation choice | Recover retained spans; extraction versions may differ | Reproduce each extraction and hash independently |\n| Apple fiscal calendar | Filings; source reading | Calendar quarters would change period context | Read policy and inline-XBRL date contexts |\n| Decimal/Fraction arithmetic | Reviewed plan; engineering choice | Avoid binary-float epsilon concealing scale errors | Independent displayed arithmetic and endpoint tests |\n| Closed half-unit rounding intervals | Reviewed hypothesis, not issuer tie rule | Conservative compatibility only; cannot identify underlying amounts | Exact interval endpoint and incompatibility tests |\n| Source-to-concept mappings | Explicit case annotations | Correct arithmetic with wrong measurement is misleading | Reject measurement/perimeter/partition substitutions |\n| Filing availability versus retained-byte vintage | SEC index and P01 | Filing dates do not date the mirrored PDF | Separate version records and unknown-cutoff tests |\n\nSource investigation, actual commands, results, changed-file hashes and the final\ndecision will be appended after implementation. No paid services, accelerator\nframeworks, package installation, model workers or background jobs are used.\n\n## Repair preflight, 2026-10-02 18:40 UTC\n\nThe interrupted implementation stopped before note records, CLI and tests existed.\nIts last failing probe constructed `RestofAsiaPacificSegmentMember`, while the\nretained HTML uses `RestOfAsiaPacificSegmentMember`. Repair this annotation from\nthe actual context, then finish the reviewed slice. The current phase-entry\ninventory contains 359 files, all still matching (the earlier 372 count above\nwas inaccurate). A separate repair baseline hashes 1,819 protected/current files\nfor the final comparison. Existing acquisitions and their failed request are\nreused; no retry or new network access is needed to inspect the retained proxy,\nannual filing and 2021 indenture. Git provenance remains unavailable.\n\nSkeptical audit passes for the repair: original disclosures remain the comparator;\n23 dispositions and arithmetic checks are bounded engineering evidence, not\nsemantic promotion. Missing anchors, wrong contexts or failed mandatory bridges\ntrigger repair before acceptance. Remaining incorporation/vintage uncertainty\nblocks only dependent claims. Existing tools suffice, and no performance or\nscientific inference is attempted. Preserve distinct P01/local interim offsets.\n\n--- files ---\nresult.md 4926 bytes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
